>
  <article class="wrap band prose-sl">
    <p>Last updated 2 November 2026.</p>
    <h2>Quotes and bookings</h2>
    <p>We quote each job before it starts. A booking is confirmed when you accept the quote and we’ve agreed how we’ll get aboard. If the boat turns out to be very different from what was described, we’ll talk to you before carrying on.</p>
    <h2>50% off your first reset</h2>
    <p>New customers get 50% off our time on their first post-trip reset, one per boat. Groceries and anything else we buy for you aren’t discounted. The discount shows on your quote, and we’ll give notice here before the offer ends.</p>
    <h2>Scope</h2>
    <p>We clean on deck and inside the boat, and we provision it to your list. We make beds with linen already on board. We don’t supply, launder or take away linen. Please take valuables off the boat, or tell us where they are.</p>
    <h2>Key holding</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We agree how we access your boat before the first job.</li>
      <li>Any key or code you give us is kept secure and is never labelled with your name, boat or berth.</li>
      <li>We only use it for jobs you’ve booked.</li>
      <li>You can ask for it back at any time. We’ll return or destroy it when you stop using the service.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Damage reporting</h2>
    <p>We take photos before and after each job. If we cause damage or notice any, we’ll tell you the same day with photos. If you spot something, tell us as soon as you can, so we can look into it properly.</p>
    <h2>Cancellation</h2>
    <p>Tell us as early as you can if your plans change. If we’ve already bought your groceries, those costs are yours, and we’ll leave them aboard or deliver them as agreed.</p>
    <h2>Weather</h2>
    <p>Safety comes first. If conditions make it unsafe to work on the boat or the pontoon, we’ll reschedule at no extra cost. A weather call is ours to make on the day.</p>
    <h2>Payment</h2>
    <p>We’ll invoice you after the job unless we agree something different.</p>
    <h2>The law</h2>
    <p>These terms sit alongside your rights under New Zealand law, including the Consumer Guarantees Act 1993 and the Fair Trading Act 1986. Nothing here takes those rights away.</p>
    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>Call or text {SITE.phoneDisplay}.</p>
  </article>
</ServicePage>
